1
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:24,980
To the shining, greatest panda,

2
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:30,960
lightly leaping over these hectic times,

3
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:37,440
diving into the city, playing the hero,

4
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,620
I wanna time with you, wanna time

5
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:42,160
nothing but the latest trends,

6
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:45,080
as we keep wearing them,

7
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,080
because your natural face
is what sells out instantly,

8
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:50,860
Let it rain

9
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:55,020
Everybody can do, we started running

10
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,240
dreams never stop, you know.

11
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,500
let's set sail for tomorrow too.

12
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,280
Let it rain

13
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:07,680
Everybody can do, just a little

14
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,820
even if we stick out, it doesn't hurt.

15
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:15,000
holding on to our rowdy curiosity,

16
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:17,380
make it stronger, make it higher.

17
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:31,180
The Bonus Battle

18
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:36,520
Now, everyone,

19
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:38,920
for many years now,

20
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:41,620
we have been plagued by one person.

21
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:43,880
That man is this one.

22
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,640
Every leader before me

23
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:53,620
took every possible measure each year
at this time to challenge this man.

24
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:54,480
But

25
00:01:54,480 --> 00:02:06,260
all of them failed, leaving us with
nothing but a heavy sense of defeat.

26
00:02:06,260 --> 00:02:08,320
Sendai was one step away.

27
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:11,020
I still haven't forgotten the
humiliation of two years ago.

28
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:14,960
Thinking about this man,
I'm so frustrated I can't sleep at night.

29
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,320
But that ends this year.

30
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,460
Now that I'm the leader, I will certainly

31
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:30,760
This year, I'll collect the debt from Kankichi Ryotsu,
no matter what!

32
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:33,740
Nyahahahaha!

33
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:39,820
Look, about that preamble you keep going on about,
you need to get to the point already.

34
00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:41,120
I understand.

35
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:48,760
So, everyone, we're now holding the strategy
meeting for the 21st Kankichi Ryotsu Bonus Contest.

36
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:53,600
Ohh, there, there, there.
It'll be over soon, okay?

37
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,155
Kikuchi, look here,

38
00:02:55,205 --> 00:02:59,220
you can't bring a baby to an
important meeting like this.

39
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:02,100
I had no choice, you see. My wife, she...

40
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:04,680
A man who can't even
collect debts is the worst.

41
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:07,480
She walked out on me, damn it.

42
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:11,556
Me, I've had my pay docked
for the delivery bills

43
00:03:11,606 --> 00:03:13,680
that Ryo-san never paid.

44
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:14,908
But honestly,

45
00:03:14,958 --> 00:03:18,900
I feel like no trick works
when you're up against Ryo-san.

46
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:22,340
What are you babbling about? Your stepfather

47
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:27,020
Dōchan, the shop owner,
as the eighth shopping district chairman,

48
00:03:27,020 --> 00:03:30,480
was risking his life collecting Ryo-san's debts,
you know.

49
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:33,560
He was passionate about everything he did.

50
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:36,420
It was Sukerokku-san who
started the sports day too.

51
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:39,680
But because of that,
he ended up with a bad back, you see.

52
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,600
Sorry, but that was a masterpiece.

53
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,140
I see.

54
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:49,700
So, this time, to snatch Ryo-san's bonus,

55
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:51,240
I've prepared a new weapon.

56
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,560
A new weapon?

57
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,420
Thirty years in the model shop business.

58
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:57,820
I poured every bit of my skill into it,

59
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:02,120
spending three months and 90% of my
effort on avoiding shopping streets.

60
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:08,600
This is the Ryo-Hunting
Base Navigation System!

61
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,120
Or Ryo-Nav for short.

62
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,340
Preparations are complete.

63
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:13,280
All that's left is to
catch Ryo-san on the day

64
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,160
and take his bonus.

65
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,700
The operation is called Operation Sky Ice.

66
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:30,100
Ryo-san, you punk, Ryotsu, Kankichi-san

67
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:30,860
Yes

68
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:33,360
Yes, this time's bonus

69
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,160
Yahoo!

70
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,160
Hehehehe

71
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,460
Looking back, 182 days without a day off

72
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:43,280
Day after day, enduring the chief's sarcasm

73
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,340
All that time spent going to the police box

74
00:04:46,978 --> 00:04:50,240
it was all for you, my dear

75
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:53,140
it was all for this adorable bonus of mine.

76
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:57,080
Ryo-san, what are you going
to spend this year's bonus on?

77
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:58,425
Well, actually,

78
00:04:58,475 --> 00:05:04,780
I've pre-ordered the limited-edition NASA special remote-control space shuttle,
1/12 scale model.

79
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:06,820
You're always like this, aren't you?

80
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:09,380
Well, guess I'll head
to the bank right away.

81
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:13,000
If I don't transfer the payment today,
it'll get canceled, you know.

82
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:29,180
There are at least thirty people here,
at a glance.

83
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:31,360
They're on higher alert than usual.

84
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,760
In that case,

85
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:35,020
Too slow.

86
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:36,980
He should be showing up any time now.

87
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,460
Didn't he already leave?

88
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:54,160
People with the sense to disguise
themselves with just sunglasses,

89
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,260
are a piece of cake.

90
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:57,940
Oh no, my bonus!

91
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,480
Excuse me, miss,

92
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,280
you dropped this.

93
00:06:03,380 --> 00:06:04,640
Thank you very much.

94
00:06:05,150 --> 00:06:06,040
Not at all.

95
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,480
W-what is it?

96
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:11,660
I thought you looked like my runaway wife,
but...

97
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:14,760
looking closer,
you're much prettier than she is!

98
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,140
How scary.

99
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:17,200
Well then,

100
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,280
take care.

101
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,680
That was close.

102
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,700
But these guys' eyes are strangely sharp,
aren't they?

103
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:23,000
Hey, Ryo-san!

104
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:25,340
You forgot your stamp!

105
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:31,800
D-damn it!

106
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,180
It's Ryo-san!

107
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:37,400
Give back my salary!
That's my money, you bastard!

108
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:40,140
Dammit!
I knew something like this would happen!

109
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:42,780
Take this!
Ninja art: Vanishing in the Clouds!

110
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:49,680
You bastard!

111
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,580
There you are! Stylish sesame!

112
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:56,580
Now then, time to claim our bonus.

113
00:07:00,260 --> 00:07:01,460
It's a ramen shop disguise!

114
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:03,160
What happened?

115
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,700
Over there!

116
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,820
When did he...?

117
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:09,020
Damn, we got beaten!

118
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:11,000
Ozaki, please respond.

119
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:13,180
This is in front of
Katsushika Police Station.

120
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:14,440
The ambush failed.

121
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,080
Ryo-san got away from us.

122
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:18,540
Begin action immediately.

123
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:19,300
Roger.

124
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:21,460
Ozaki, are you all right?

125
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:24,800
We expected Ryo-san to escape at this stage.

126
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,620
Now the real Sky Eye operation begins.

127
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:32,840
It's built in.

128
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:38,240
the satellite catches that signal

129
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,580
so we can always know where he is.

130
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,640
It's all gibberish to me.

131
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:46,340
Will this really work?

132
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:48,900
It's the same system the
US military uses in Japan.

133
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:51,680
The reliability is over 200%.

134
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:55,320
But I just can't trust new machines.

135
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:56,040
Yeah, yeah.

136
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:58,520
This time, Granny,
you can just sit back and watch.

137
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,340
Sky Eye activated. Starting operation.

138
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:10,400
What's this glowing dot?

139
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,100
That's Ryo-san's current location.

140
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:15,080
The target is taking the back streets

141
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:17,160
and heading for Kameari General Bank.

142
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:19,300
We'll get ahead of him and lie in wait.

143
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:19,980
Roger.

144
00:08:19,980 --> 00:08:23,320
Ryo-san, it's no use running anywhere.

145
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:26,500
Your location is being watched from the sky.

146
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:33,220
Welcome!

147
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:35,280
Come on in and have a look!

148
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:37,920
Be sure to spend your bonus
at the Kameari Shopping Street!

149
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,340
Damn, they got ahead of us!

150
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:48,220
Alright! Street Riders, move out!

151
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:51,440
Good luck!

152
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,060
Damn it!

153
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:58,260
Time to show what my bike skills,
honed every day, can do!

154
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,940
He even got himself a bike!

155
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:01,240
In that case!

156
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:06,440
What?

157
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:11,800
You're too quick!

158
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:14,200
You're too naive, Ryo-san!

159
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:16,620
It was...

160
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:19,480
I've heard it so many times it's
practically stuck in my ears.

161
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:20,420
Hey!

162
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:24,580
Aaaaaah!

163
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:25,080
Aaaaah!

164
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:25,760
Woooah!

165
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:29,880
Hello?

166
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:31,720
Street Riders

167
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:32,900
wiped out.

168
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:36,500
across the Nakagawa.

169
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:37,880
He's trying to get to the next town.

170
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,620
Ryo-san is heading for the next town.

171
00:09:40,620 --> 00:09:41,940
At the middle of the bridge!

172
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:42,980
Pincer him!

173
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:47,260
Damn it, they're really fired up this year!

174
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:52,460
It's safer to leave the neighborhood
and head for the bank in the next town.

175
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,800
We're not letting you through here, Ryo-san.

176
00:10:00,220 --> 00:10:03,500
N-no way,
how did they know to block this spot?

177
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:09,700
Ryo-san, there's no way out.

178
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:11,780
What on earth is going on?

179
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:14,800
Bonus for me!

180
00:10:14,860 --> 00:10:17,180
Bonus! Give me the bonus!

181
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,580
Everyone!

182
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:23,000
Bonus! Bonus! Bonus!

183
00:10:23,020 --> 00:10:28,200
Bonus! Bonus! Bonus!

184
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,960
No way I'm letting that happen!

185
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:39,980
He actually jumped into the
river in the dead of winter!

186
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,240
He's getting away!

187
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:45,380
Wait, you...

188
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:47,520
Hey, we're human, you know!

189
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:50,060
If we jump into this freezing water,
we'll die!

190
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:52,280
Look!

191
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:56,800
What the hell are you doing?

192
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:04,620
Is this shabby gateball the one you dropped?

193
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:07,340
Or is it Shigeo
Nagashima's autographed ball?

194
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,680
Nagashima's autographed ball.

195
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:11,700
Obviously it's a gateball, you idiot!

196
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:13,960
Let me borrow a light.

197
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:17,951
Damn it,

198
00:11:18,001 --> 00:11:21,460
how on earth do they always
know exactly where I'm going?

199
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:26,540
What is this cord?

200
00:11:28,420 --> 00:11:30,600
A battery inside the handcuff case?

201
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:35,200
So you were monitoring me
with a navigation system?

202
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:36,900
You've come up with quite a plan.

203
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:39,200
But I'm not going to be caught that easily!

204
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:43,730
I have an important mission:

205
00:11:43,780 --> 00:11:46,362
to go to the bank today and transfer money

206
00:11:46,412 --> 00:11:48,020
so my radio-controlled model
pre-order doesn't get cancelled!

207
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:49,640
Idiot! Idiot!

208
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:51,000
Who are you calling an idiot?!

209
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,020
Idiot! Idiot!

210
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:54,460
Yeah, that's right!

211
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:57,120
Heh heh heh heh heh heh heh!

212
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:05,247
I'm not so fragile that jumping
into a river would break me,

213
00:12:05,297 --> 00:12:06,680
the navigator I built!

214
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:10,140
Is this really showing Ryo-san's location?

215
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:13,060
I honestly don't trust it.

216
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:15,000
Hey.

217
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:16,740
Chief Ohara.

218
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:17,940
How does it look?

219
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,700
Has Ryotsu been caught?

220
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:20,960
It's only a matter of time.

221
00:12:21,340 --> 00:12:24,200
This is all thanks to your cooperation,
Chief Ohara.

222
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:26,080
Swapping Ryotsu's belt is

223
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,520
child's play.

224
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:42,300
Because of that guy any more,

225
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:45,400
I can't let you all be troubled any further.

226
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:48,500
No, no, please,
just rest easy and leave it to us.

227
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,760
Thank you in advance.

228
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:50,860
Mr. Ozaki.

229
00:12:50,860 --> 00:12:52,380
What is it, old lady?

230
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:54,960
It suddenly stopped moving a while ago.

231
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:56,640
Didn't it break?

232
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,300
That's impossible.

233
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:01,660
Shut it.

234
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:04,200
Looks like he's worn out from
running and is taking a breather.

235
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:08,020
Chief Ohara,
we're about to show you Ryo-san's end.

236
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:09,700
Is it finally time?

237
00:13:09,700 --> 00:13:10,800
Come on, get in.

238
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:11,300
Yes.

239
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:18,580
Backup is on the way, backup is on the way.

240
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:21,900
Ryo-san is currently hiding
in the Kameari Hybrid Hotel.

241
00:13:22,280 --> 00:13:24,020
We're going all in right here.

242
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:27,860
From now on,
Operation Sky Eye enters its final phase.

243
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:30,020
Everyone, head for the hotel!

244
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:37,540
Aaaaaaah!

245
00:13:37,540 --> 00:13:37,620
Aaaaaaah!

246
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:42,420
Is Ryo-san really here?

247
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:44,460
Trust in the latest technology.

248
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,680
This optional CD-ROM

249
00:13:49,680 --> 00:13:51,820
syncs with the signal from the satellite

250
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:53,620
and instantly, within the hotel,

251
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:55,660
will pinpoint Ryo-san's location.

252
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,100
This room

253
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:00,620
Attention, all units!

254
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:03,540
Ryo-san is on the balcony of Room 817.

255
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,580
From the balcony of Room 816,

256
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,440
Team B, from the balcony of Room 818,

257
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:14,760
Teams C and D,
break in through the inside of Room 817!

258
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:19,640
The fate of the Kameari shopping
street rests on this battle.

259
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:23,180
All teams, rally your spirits!
Be sure to win!

260
00:14:23,180 --> 00:14:25,800
Yuki, we're finally alone.

261
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:26,420
Here we go.

262
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,720
Team B is in position.

263
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,040
Team B, go ahead.

264
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:44,080
Team B is in position on
the balcony of Room 818.

265
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:45,860
Teams C and D,

266
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:48,180
Teams C and D are also in position.

267
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:49,440
Copy that.

268
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:51,600
Starting countdown.

269
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,440
Five.

270
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:53,740
Four.

271
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:55,140
Three.

272
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:56,240
Two.

273
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,380
One.

274
00:14:57,380 --> 00:14:58,640
Move in!

275
00:15:08,180 --> 00:15:10,940
Report. Did we capture the target?

276
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:12,380
It's a crow.

277
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:13,120
A crow?

278
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:20,140
The one on the balcony isn't Ryo-san.
It's a crow wearing Ryo-san's belt.

279
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:22,860
No way...

280
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:25,860
Of all things,
our belt-swap plan got foiled.

281
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:31,380
That's why I said you can't trust machines.

282
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:36,000
Looks like I won again this year.

283
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,720
Well then,
time to finally rake in the big money.

284
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:47,920
There's money lying on the ground!

285
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:48,420
Money?

286
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,580
Money, money, money, money.

287
00:15:51,580 --> 00:15:55,820
Found it! Got it!

288
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:58,820
Kids' bank?

289
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,480
Dammit! You tricked me, you sneaky bastard!

290
00:16:04,820 --> 00:16:08,660
Hey, we could've caught him easily
without using machines, right?

291
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:11,940
Y-yeah, for Ryo-san,
this method might be the best.

292
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:13,220
Just as expected of an old hand.

293
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:14,515
How pathetic.

294
00:16:14,565 --> 00:16:19,680
What was all my hard work for?!

295
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:23,552
Come on, line up, line up!

296
00:16:23,602 --> 00:16:26,300
Then, is it all right, Chief Ohara?

297
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:28,980
Go ahead, go ahead, please take it.

298
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:31,040
Thanks, Ryo-san, we'll take it.

299
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:32,780
What's the matter?

300
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,560
You're awfully meek, aren't you?

301
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:37,100
No, it's the one who doesn't
pay their tab that's to blame.

302
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:39,000
Don't hold back, take it.

303
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:39,920
I see.

304
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:42,840
Being told so casually really throws me off

305
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:43,960
Sorry, Sachiko.

306
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:48,320
Looks like it'll be a long time
before I can come and get you.

307
00:16:48,820 --> 00:16:49,740
Who's that girl?

308
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:51,260
She's my little sister, Sachiko.

309
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:53,200
Sachiko's hands and feet are numb

310
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:57,500
from working in a northern place
so cold it freezes you to the bone.

311
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:00,520
Working? She's still a child!

312
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:06,820
It's a long story, one I'll never forget.

313
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:10,740
Sachiko was born on a snowy, cold night.

314
00:17:10,740 --> 00:17:14,560
Dad and Mom were overjoyed.

315
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:17,860
Hoping she'd grow up to be a happy child,

316
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:19,740
we named her Sachiko.

317
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:21,020
But...

318
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:38,920
Our parents died in a sudden accident, and on top of that,
the insurance money we were supposed to get was swindled away by a crooked broker.

319
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:45,360
To make matters worse, our house collapsed.

320
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:52,340
On top of that, we found out our late parents' business
had failed and left us with 200 million yen in debt.

321
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:56,920
Sachiko was taken away by a relative
who said they'd take on the debt.

322
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:58,620
But then,

323
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,520
that relative turned out to be

324
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:03,040
the president of a shady
construction company.

325
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:06,080
He's even forcing little Sachiko to work.

326
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:08,680
She barely gets enough to eat,

327
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:11,120
so I tried to take Sachiko back somehow,

328
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:13,880
but every time, he waved the 200
million yen debt contract in my face.

329
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,860
That's when I made up my mind.

330
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,680
If I just kept earning
money steadily the normal way,

331
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:21,460
it wouldn't be enough
before Sachiko comes of age.

332
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,460
Every last yen of my salary and bonuses

333
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:25,940
will go straight toward paying off the debt.

334
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:31,420
I don't care how much people
in the world resent me for it.

335
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:37,420
But Big Brother was wrong.

336
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:39,660
Even though you've had a hard time,

337
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:43,140
I never realized you'd caused this
much trouble for so many people.

338
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:46,080
Big Brother is a disgrace as a human being.

339
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:50,740
I see. So that's how it was.

340
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:55,600
Not knowing that, I called you human scum.
Please forgive me.

341
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:57,240
How heartless.

342
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:00,640
Everyone, perhaps his methods were wrong,

343
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:02,720
but in his own way,

344
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:05,620
he was trying to live his
life as a decent human being.

345
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:06,929
Please,

346
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:10,440
for the sake of Daijiro Ohara here,
please forgive us.

347
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:12,840
It's us who were forgiven.

348
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:14,700
Without even considering
Ryo-san's situation,

349
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:17,740
we were trying to snatch your bonus.

350
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:20,360
Here, Ryo-san, this is your bonus.

351
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:22,700
Hurry and get it to your little sister.

352
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:24,780
B-but this is...

353
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:29,600
The debt can be paid back whenever, too.

354
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:31,840
Compared to Ryo-san's situation,

355
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:34,180
we're a million times happier.

356
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:35,280
Sounds good.

357
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:36,680
Don't lose.

358
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:40,520
We'll never forget your
kindness as long as we live.

359
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:43,360
I'm sure my little sister will be happy too.

360
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,380
Hey, everyone.

361
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:51,080
What's all this, then?

362
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,040
What's this?

363
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,860
That's Ryotsu's little sister, Sachiko!

364
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,400
This is a magazine clipping, though.

365
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:02,080
Besides, Senpai doesn't have
a younger sister, does he?

366
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:08,220
If you fall for a story like that...

367
00:20:08,220 --> 00:20:11,220
Steal my bonus?
That's absolutely impossible.

368
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:12,400
Thank you very much.

369
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:16,240
Now all that's left is to go to the bank.

370
00:20:20,540 --> 00:20:21,680
Whoa, what is this?

371
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,860
Who the hell did this?

372
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:28,584
Going by this data,

373
00:20:28,634 --> 00:20:31,207
after you shake off our pursuit,

374
00:20:31,257 --> 00:20:34,380
there's a 95% chance you'll
take a break at this café.

375
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:39,500
Just as I thought.
Waiting in ambush was worth it.

376
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:42,400
Model shop owner,
what on earth is that outfit!

377
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:45,720
This is the anti-Ryotsu
citrus-type debt collection weapon,

378
00:20:45,770 --> 00:20:47,080
the Debt Gresx.

379
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:48,920
It's the Debt Gresx!

380
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:53,308
We've been secretly developing
it for next year's bonus battle,

381
00:20:53,358 --> 00:20:55,020
and it's always 80% finished.

382
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:58,640
But you should be able to defeat it.

383
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:19,320
Well -

384
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:33,060
this month

385
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:35,160
Rest assured.

386
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:37,160
Taking your stamina into account,

387
00:21:37,160 --> 00:21:40,060
I've set the voltage just
low enough that you won't die.

388
00:21:40,060 --> 00:21:42,940
You'll probably pass out, though.

389
00:21:42,940 --> 00:21:47,220
Electric shot!

390
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:50,760
Shot!

391
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:56,360
My bonus!

392
00:21:56,900 --> 00:21:59,200
I don't want to resort
to such rough measures,

393
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:02,740
but it's your fault for not
paying your debts willingly.

394
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:05,020
Well then, let's collect that bonus.

395
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:08,860
What's wrong?

396
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,640
So close, yet so far.

397
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:25,900
Now you understand, right?

398
00:22:25,900 --> 00:22:28,880
There's no way you lot can take my bonus.

399
00:22:29,620 --> 00:22:33,460
Even if the Chief forgives you, God won't.

400
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:40,980
Sure enough, even God...

401
00:22:40,980 --> 00:22:41,860
Wait!

402
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:43,700
Wait, wait!

403
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:45,420
Don't come any closer!

404
00:22:45,420 --> 00:22:47,720
Look, there's no shutter!

405
00:22:47,720 --> 00:22:49,500
Oh no, that's bad.

406
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:52,460
Aaaaaaah!

407
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:08,520
What is Ryotsu doing?

408
00:23:15,420 --> 00:23:20,540
Even if it turns to ash, as long as the original shape of the bill remains,
the bank will exchange it.

409
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,740
What a touching effort.

410
00:23:22,740 --> 00:23:27,360
Hey, if you're really willing to pay off your debts that way,
I'll help you.

411
00:23:27,360 --> 00:23:31,340
Don't talk to me.
This job requires concentration.

412
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,620
My bonus.

413
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:49,480
Next year's bonus,
I'll definitely snatch it for sure.

414
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:50,980
Ryotsu Kankichi!

415
00:24:05,220 --> 00:24:06,100
I did it!

416
00:24:06,100 --> 00:24:06,898
So,

417
00:24:06,948 --> 00:24:12,160
In the Katsushika station survey, I finally beat that
Nakagawa and was chosen as the most popular officer.

418
00:24:12,460 --> 00:24:14,970
A man isn't about face or body, you know.

419
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:17,240
It's the heart, the heart. Get it?

420
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:21,100
Next time: Ryotsu's Super Popular Declaration.
See you then.

421
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:37,760
Because it all passes by,

422
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:42,700
don't go around with a sour face.

423
00:24:44,380 --> 00:24:47,960
Let's laugh it off and keep on living.

424
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:53,020
Even if today

425
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:57,920
is a rainy day,

426
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:03,440
tomorrow will be sunny.

427
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:05,320
Bye-bye!

428
00:25:06,140 --> 00:25:13,820
Let's wave goodbye to the unpleasant things.

429
00:25:13,820 --> 00:25:23,960
Oh yeah, let's live the way we like,
good things are coming!

430
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:30,220
Outside the door, the stars are calling you.

431
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

